o get pixel-perfect via API for complex screens. I'll use a mix: fixed-position frames for the main screen (414×896) with absolutely positioned sections, but use auto-layout inside components (rows, chips). Actually auto-layout everywhere makes text sizing predictable. I'll use auto-layout for rows/cards, absolute for screen composition. Screens may scroll vertically — in a static design, content that overflows is clipped; I should design content to fit nicely within 896 or let it overflow with clipContent=true (representing scroll). 02_Home has a lot of content: header(~60)+search(~50)+title(~40)+categories(~150)+recommendation(~200)+today(~110)+tabbar(90) ≈ 800 + paddings — fits roughly. 03_Warm_Up: hero(~300)+title/tags(~90)+desc(~60)+exercises header(~40)+10 rows(~76 each = 760) → definitely overflows 896. That's fine: it's a scroll view; the frame clips. The tab bar must be fixed at bottom overlay. I'll set frame clipsContent true and place tab bar absolutely at bottom over content. Content extends beyond frame bottom and is clipped — visually communicates scroll. The brief says \"may scroll vertically\" — so overflow is expected and acceptable. But for the screenshot, the visible portion should look complete. Good.\n\nLet me now inspect things. First read workspace page + component internals via use_figma read-only (return JSON of properties). Keep code within limits.\n\nNote: the tool says call get_design_context — not available in my toolset; use_figma inspection is the equivalent. Fine.\n\nAlso I must read the skill guidance: \"Before calling this tool, load figma-use guidance — prefer the /figma-use skill if available, otherwise read the skill://figma/figma-use/SKILL.md MCP resource if available.\" I don't have a resource-reading tool listed... The MCP resources aren't accessible via my tools (no read-resource tool). I have no skills directory access? There might be a /figma-use skill — but I only have the four figma tools plus none for skills. I cannot re