but brief says show exercises 1-10 — a screenshot check might penalize missing rows.\n\nAlternative: two-column grid of exercise cards: cell 179×110: photo thumb 179×?? no.\n\nOr: reduce to row height via component scale: create rows as instances but place in a scroll-indicating container and shrink spacing: rows 52, gap 4 → 10*52+9*4=556; start 456 → ends 1012. no.\n\nWhat about making the exercise list 2 columns × 5 rows: each cell 179×52 with name+duration only, thumb 36, play hidden? Cell width 179: thumb 32 + name/dur. Names like \"Tabletop Kick\" SB12 fits ~100px? ok. 5 rows of 52 + gaps 8 → 292 → 456+292 = 748 < 806 ✓. But component is 366 wide — instance resize(179,52) with auto-layout: FILL info shrinks ✓ (auto-layout handles). Play circle 32 stays; total min width ~ 6+32+8+info+8+32 = tight but ok. Duration text '02.30' short. Info FILL min... Name \"Tabletop Kick\" SB13 ≈ 90px. 32+8+90+8+32+12pad = 182 > 179 slight overflow → set name SB12 or duration shorter '02.30'. Fine-tune: set Info min width? Just try; adjust font sizes via override.\n\nHmm, but 2-col grid loses the \"play small\" look? Keep play circle.\n\nActually simpler: keep single column list but move 'Exercises' section up and compress hero: hero 220; title y 240; chips y 280; desc y 322 (2 lines, ends 362); Exercises y 378; rows y 412, gap 6, h 44?? Component fixed 52h... \n\nWhat if I resize rows to (366, 48) and gap 4? If auto-layout vertical center with padding 6: thumb 40 → 48-12=36 available... children fixed size 40 thumb > 36 → auto-layout doesn't clip, it just overflows/stretches container? Auto-layout hug? Row fixed 366×52; resize to 48 → children positioned per alignment; thumb 40 centered vertically ok (padding effectively 4). Play 32 ok. Looks fine actually! Auto-layout with FIXED primary and FIXED counter: resizing counter axis to 48: children align per counterAxisAlignItems CENTER → thumb 40 at y4. OK!\n\nRows 48h gap 4: 10*48+9*4 = 516. Start y: minimize upper: hero 224; title